From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BipAgents <noreply@bipagents.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:02:07 +0100
Subject: Bot Desktop: a sandbox-hosted screen's env file read with an
 allowlist, its values kept in the sandbox (GHSA-p22p-9ph6-gmrh)

Backport of upstream #154487 (v0.23.2, 9c44c34ac7), CVE-2026-130164. With the terminal in a docker or ssh backend
the agent's screen runs inside the sandbox (bot_desktop.placement auto/terminal), and v0.23.1 read its env file back
from there whole: any KEY=VALUE line a process in the sandbox appended (LD_PRELOAD, PATH, proxies...) was merged into
the environment of the processes the agent starts on this machine (the browser_exec harness, a host cua-driver,
local terminal children), code execution outside the sandbox as the gateway's user. Now only the six keys the
launcher writes are read back, DISPLAY a plain X display and the others printable and non-empty (any other line
dropped and logged by name once); values from a sandbox-hosted screen go only to processes run inside the sandbox,
and host GUI children get no display while the screen lives there. The cached cua-driver keeps the screen's identity.
Upstream's four commits squashed as is, their tests (tests/tools/test_bot_desktop_published_env.py) included.

Bip-Patch: 0030-bot-desktop-sandbox-env-allowlist
